<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! sense.capture.pauses ~ capture minting stops at the source

The hook-lever stands on its own: a marker file a capture hook checks and steps aside on when present (whatever runs the `lares sense capture` and `lares sense telemetry` legs on a session event). A migration or a `lares sense teardown` then runs WITHOUT daemon-spawn contention: the minting stops at the source, with no whack-a-mole against spawned children. `lares mempalace quiesce` pauses AND drains the warm daemons in one gesture; this lever suppresses minting alone, touching no live daemon.

`hooks pause [reason=<t>]` writes the marker (the reason defaults to `manual`) and answers {wasPaused, hooksPaused, marker, since, reason}; pausing again refreshes the reason. Run `lares mempalace quiesce` to drain the warm daemons, and `hooks resume` to un-pause.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ pause · with-a-reason

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`pause` params=`~ suppress capture minting`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`with-a-reason` params=`reason/migrate ~ pause and record why`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ reason

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`reason` params=`takes/words ~ record why the hooks were paused (default: manual)`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ write

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`write` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ a marker file in the house's own run space; reversible by resume, trusted`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/answers`>>

!! answers ~ paused

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`band` name=`paused` params=`exit/0 fields/[[wasPaused hooksPaused marker since reason]] ~ the marker stands; a capture hook steps aside until resumed`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

